test.yaml:13:3: job "final" reads "needs.*.result" but has no "if" with a status check function, so GitHub skips the job when a job it needs fails or is skipped, and a skipped job counts as passing for a required check. add "if: ${{ !cancelled() }}" (or "always()") to the job [gate-job-skipped-on-failure]
test.yaml:21:9: job "notify" reads "needs.build.result" but its "if" has no status check function, so GitHub skips the job when a job it needs fails or is skipped, and a skipped job counts as passing for a required check. add "!cancelled()" or "always()" to the condition [gate-job-skipped-on-failure]
test.yaml:25:3: job "report" reads "needs" but has no "if" with a status check function, so GitHub skips the job when a job it needs fails or is skipped, and a skipped job counts as passing for a required check. add "if: ${{ !cancelled() }}" (or "always()") to the job [gate-job-skipped-on-failure]
